The adaptation in src/chemistry/abbreviations/replacement.rs specializes the
algorithm to two finite coordinate differences, preserving math.hypot rounding
when placing fixed abbreviation templates. It uses safe Rust and does not
include or invoke the Python interpreter.

The adaptations in src/chemistry/cdxml/marks.rs and
src/chemistry/cdxml/arrows.rs preserve native chemical-symbol sizes and arrow
geometry acceptance thresholds. The arrow specialization also retains
subnormal scaling and infinity/NaN handling. Both use safe Rust without
including or invoking the Python interpreter.

The specialization in src/chemistry/cdxml/graphics/shapes.rs preserves
chemical-symbol size thresholds using the same compensated norm in safe Rust.

The adaptation in src/chemistry/cdxml/scene/circles.rs follows the compensated
float summation in Python/bltinmodule.c, builtin_sum_impl, from the same pinned
CPython release. Together with the arrow norm specialization, it preserves the
original aromatic-circle ownership thresholds without invoking Python.

The adaptation in src/chemistry/cleanup/numeric.rs uses the same compensated
float summation from Python/bltinmodule.c, builtin_sum_impl, to preserve
selection cleanup orientation. Its norm calculations reuse the audited arrow
specialization; neither operation includes or invokes the Python interpreter.
